  "notes": "Leimert Park cool-rap — the low-BPM, sample-warm, non-club end of 2010s LA, and the same \"crawling drums\" rule as Nipsey: **snare and clap placed audibly late**, kick soft, hats thin or absent, swing present but small. Harmony comes from the sample source, so 7th and 9th colours rather than triads, and the progressions are real (`Imaj7–vi7–ii7–V`). Verse-dominant forms with no hook at all, which is why the countermelody is a sung/spoken layer rather than a lead.",
